schema: "0.4"
id: npl-blueprint-14-admin-llm-model-catalog
type: image
quality: high

# NoizuPromptLingo (structured prompt-definition language + MCP agent toolchain) — Admin: LLM Model Catalog screen.
# Theme tenets: cool drafting sheet, faint grid texture, thin cyan rules + monospace annotations, near-square 2px corners, one warm redline for markup.
# Palette: sheet #f5f8fc, navy ink #14263f, blueprint-blue #245ea8, drafting cyan #0e9bd6, redline #c05a3e.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity UI mockup of a
    platform-administration surface for NoizuPromptLingo — a structured
    prompt-definition language and MCP agent toolchain. The register is a
    technical drafting sheet: cool, exacting, calm — "drawn by someone who
    measures twice." Structure is the aesthetic — a faint background grid, thin
    cyan rules, dimension lines, and monospace callout labels do the work.
    Engineered IBM Plex Sans for UI, IBM Plex Mono for every precise value.
    Near-square corners, nearly flat surfaces, no gradients or glow. The only
    warm color is a single red-oxide redline reserved for markup and attention.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity UI mockup of the Admin: LLM Model Catalog screen of
    NoizuPromptLingo — a platform-wide catalog of available LLM providers and
    models with live connectivity testing before a model is offered to
    organizations.

    OVERALL LAYOUT (two bands over a faint blueprint grid): a slim LEFT ADMIN NAV
    RAIL that reads like a sheet index (thin cyan active left-rule, small mono
    section labels), and a dominant CENTER work area split into a catalog table on
    the left and an add-provider form on the right. A monospace breadcrumb path
    "admin / llm-models" and a title "Model Catalog" in medium-weight sans sit at
    the top.

    MODEL CATALOG TABLE (main card, title-block header "Providers & models"): a
    dense table with a cyan dimension-line under 500-weight sans column headers
    (Provider, Model ID, Health, Enabled orgs). A monospace Model ID column
    (provider/model-name), quiet cool-hairline row separators, and a faint cyan
    row-hover tint. A PROVIDER HEALTH BADGE per row: last-known connectivity as a
    small dimension chip — teal-green with a check glyph for reachable, warm
    redline with a warning glyph for failing (status is glyph-paired, never color
    alone). An Enabled-orgs column shows a monospace count.

    ADD MODEL PROVIDER FORM (right card, title-block header "Add provider"):
    fields with small monospace dimension-labels above — provider name, a
    monospace endpoint URL field on the grid, and a masked credential/API-key
    field. A blueprint-blue LIVE CONNECTIVITY TEST BUTTON labeled "Test
    connection" with, just beneath it, an inline pass result — a teal-green "200 ·
    reachable" line in monospace paired with a check glyph — shown before saving.
    A blueprint-blue primary "Save provider" button at the bottom.

    PALETTE & TYPE: a pale cool drafting-sheet canvas carrying dark navy drafting
    ink. Structure is blueprint blue; thin rules and highlights are a drafting
    cyan; a single warm red-oxide redline is reserved for failing health and
    attention — the red pencil on a blue drawing. Success reads as a calm
    teal-green, always paired with a glyph. Neutrals are cool-tinted toward blue,
    never warm, never pure gray. Engineered IBM Plex Sans for UI and body; IBM
    Plex Mono carries every precise value — model identifiers, endpoint URLs,
    status codes, counts, and the small callout labels above fields.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: near-square corners — drawn, not soft, not stamped. Borders
    are the drawing: thin single-pixel cyan and blueprint-blue rules form every
    cell divider, panel edge, and dimension line; surfaces are the paper between
    them. Nearly flat — cards rest on a rule and a faint tone step, never a drop
    shadow. The faint blueprint grid sits under the whole canvas, static and
    low-contrast.

    MOOD: precise, technical, trustworthy within five seconds. Cool, exacting,
    calm — a configuration surface drawn on an engineer's drafting table where
    correctness and legibility of structure matter more than warmth.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Matches Admin: LLM Model Catalog — a provider/model table with per-row health badges, an add-provider form, and a live connectivity test with inline pass/fail"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Cool drafting sheet, faint blueprint grid, thin cyan/blueprint-blue rules, monospace values, near-square corners, glyph-paired teal/redline status — not generic UI defaults"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Clear visual hierarchy, plausible real-product admin layout with title-block cards"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"

tags: [npl-blueprint, NoizuPromptLingo, screen-mockup]
